  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We can replace <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> charge at origin by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now due to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> charge at every corner of cube. Electric field at center of cube is zero so now net electric field at center is only due to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> charge at origin.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
